mechanisms={
 'S1':('28d+1h; >=4 subject baseline activities','Current wallet subject','Split a total drawn log-uniform USD 100..1000 by Dirichlet weights with alpha independently U(0.5,2) for each payment; spread over U(5,75) minutes. Both short-window and dispersed longer opportunities occur.','Use the same total/count law, with one random Dirichlet alpha=8 and others=1, or duration U(45,120) minutes (equal choice).','S1 max-share, count, value and acceleration; an early event need not satisfy the full conjunction.','Shared rounding/type rules; avoid an origin-specific total or cents signature.'),
 'S2':('35d; >=4 subject baseline activities','Current wallet subject','Draw anchor log-uniform USD 30..500; choose log jitter SD U(0.005,0.02) or U(0.02,0.15) with equal probability. Payments span U(1,7)d with ordinary context. No current-centered membership is consulted while sampling.','Use the same anchor/jitter mixture and repeated focal-wallet schedule; half use an amount drawn from a strictly prior subject payment if available, otherwise the ordinary recipe anchor. Existing prior repetition may defeat growth.','S2 5% tolerance, cluster count/value/share and baseline cluster growth.','Narrow jitter is an explicit challenge assumption, not a target-derived positive filter; audit cents/amount associations.'),
 'S3':('UTC midnight minus 28d; >=4 baseline activities','Current wallet subject','Distribute payments over U(3,24)h using independent uniform timestamps; midnight crossing is permitted.','Same time/amount law with half the events assigned to each of two random instants within the interval; timestamps retain full-key ordering.','S3 occupied hours, current-day count/value and daily-median growth.','No day-total future lookup; report midnight and same-time ties separately.'),
 'S4':('35d; >=4 subject baseline activities','Current wallet subject','Every motif amount is an independent Stage 15A LARGE_CONDITIONAL proposal; duration U(1,7)d. More motif slots per episode improve opportunity density without changing amount support or band thresholds.','Identical conditional amount law; evenly spaced times within the same random duration and preference for an active recurring-payment subject. No cloned amount or forced negative.','S4 current band, count/share/variation and relative band activity.','Recipe support is wider than target band. Fresh proposals, identical precision and conditional shift for both origins; exact band yield remains uncertain.'),
 'N1':('29d; >=4 prior incoming baseline W2W edges','Current W2W receiver','Choose receiver, DU(2,8) distinct senders and cycle them for M W2W payments over U(1,30)h; anchors use shared network amount law.','Use DU(1,3) senders or prefer previously observed sender relationships with equal probability; same time/value law.','N1 24h count, >=3 senders, value and incoming growth.','No collection-profile label; sparse incoming eligibility remains a risk.'),
 'N2':('29d; >=4 prior outgoing baseline W2W edges','Current W2W sender','Mirror N1 with a focal sender and DU(2,8) receivers over U(1,30)h.','Same values/timing with DU(1,3) receivers or observed recurring recipients; no negative override.','N2 24h count, breadth, value and outgoing growth.','Preserve N2 despite adequate development counts; collection/dispersion types must not identify labels.'),
 'N3':('Strictly prior 7d; no baseline minimum','Current W2W endpoints','V=DU(2,6), K=DU(0,2), M=V+K. Primary walk plus return; K adds a parallel prior edge or alternative two-edge route as Stage 15A. Amount first log-uniform USD 30..500; adjacent factors log-uniform 0.2..5; closing/first factor U(0.2,1.4). Duration U(1h,7d). Choose chronological order or swap two primary prior edge times with equal probability where at least two exist. Extra-route times uniform before proposed closing instant.','Same topology/value support; chronological swap probability 0.75. For one-edge prior routes the swap is inapplicable and recorded; no retry.','N3 any simple chronological 1..5 prior-edge return path and all frozen amount ratios.','Do not select a path by target qualification. Full enumeration required; no feature containing qualifying-path count. Same amount law for hard and ordinary graph motifs.'),
 'N4':('Prior 24h incoming-W2W anchor; no long baseline','Outward W2W sender or cash-out wallet','One incoming W2W funding amount log-uniform USD 30..1000, then M-1 outward events; total outward proposal fraction U(0.1,1.2), Dirichlet(1) shares, half cash-out/half W2W independently. Duration U(1,30)h.','Same funding law; fraction U(0.1,0.6), same schema and mixed outward law. Other prior funding remains real and may change results.','N4 F>=USD100, half-to-full outward fraction and residual funding.','Funding proposal alone is not positive; do not use future exits to label it.'),
 'A1':('35d; >=12 baseline services','Current agent and serviced wallets','Duration U(2,28)d; regular-catchment probability U(0.2,0.9), service opportunity multiplier U(0.8,2.5). Existing ordinary acquisition/retention/shocks remain active; recent breadth and newness arise from actual history.','Half prefer already observed active customers, half use the ordinary acquisition mixture. Promotion, migration, seasonality and recovery never override labels.','A1 D>=6, U>=4, U/D>=0.5 and growth>=1.5, unchanged.','Keep A1 as a target component; high accuracy or growth importance is not automatically leakage.'),
 'A2':('29d; >=20 baseline services and >=5 wallets','Current agent','DU(2,6) active customers receive share U(0.35,0.95); others receive remaining share. Duration U(2,30)h.','Select frequent prior customers when available using same share law and duration; otherwise ordinary active selection with logged fallback.','A2 >=8 recent services, top2>=0.65 and change>=0.2.','Stable concentration can fail change; agent identity/provenance cannot enter X.'),
 'A3':('28d+1h; >=12 baseline services','Current agent','DU(2,8) customers and duration U(0.25,3)h; uniform event times; ordinary service types.','Same law with DU(1,3) customers or duration U(0.75,3)h, equal choice.','A3 recent count, breadth and acceleration against 1h-offset baseline.','No family-specific ID blocks or deterministic time bins; longer bursts can miss the recent count.'),
 'A4':('29d; >=12 baseline services including >=8 cash','Current cash-service agent','DU(2,8) wallets; draw cash-out probability U(0.1,0.9), assign directions independently, amounts from shared BASE with out-direction multiplier U(0.5,2), duration U(2,30)h.','Same probability magnitude oriented toward prior observed dominant cash direction if available; otherwise same ordinary probability. No target inspection.','A4 cash count/breadth, signed count/value skew agreement and historical skew change.','Amounts and counts may disagree. No accept-until-imbalance or forced cash direction label.')}

