write('challenge_hard_negative_spec.json',{'families':hard,'scope':'Twelve matched strata retain all H1-H8 concepts; H1 covers S1/S3, H2 S2, H3 S4, H4 N1, H5 N2/N4, H6 N3, H7 A1/A3, H8 A2/A4. Origin is private and not a class.','near_boundary_slice':'Post-generation diagnostic only: applicable family with required historical eligibility and exactly one numeric atomic condition failing. Counts are within 1 below a lower bound; ratios within 10% of the fixed positive threshold on the failing side. For upper bounds use 10% above. S4 amount outside band within 5% of its endpoint; exact sign/variation failures reported separately. N3: topology present but every route fails full monetary conjunction; report separately without claiming a unique closest path. N4 missing anchor reported separately, not called a near numeric boundary. Union target0 is required for FPR; otherwise count cross-family positives. No slice definition affects sampling.'})

policy={'family_objectives':{f:{'positive_decision_points':200,'distinct_subjects':40,'episode_or_background_clusters':50,'local_units':12,'minimum_positive_rows_in_each_of_at_least_4_fixed_30day_bins':20,'max_subject_share':0.10,'max_unit_share':0.20,'max_30day_bin_share':0.40,'per_arm_positive_points':80,'per_arm_units':8} for f in family},
 'negative_objectives':{f:{'union_target0_matched_hard_rows':200,'distinct_subjects':30,'local_units':12,'near_boundary_target0_rows':50,'near_boundary_units':8} for f in family},
 'rationale':'200 independent Bernoulli observations have worst-case normal-approximation 95% half-width 1.96*sqrt(.25/200)=0.0693. This is only planning intuition; correlation worsens precision. Forty subjects, fifty episode/day clusters and twelve represented units guard concentration, not a claimed effective sample size. Each arm has twelve available unit clusters, so arm comparisons remain exploratory and uncertainty may be wide. Do not claim the original 300-row policy has been relaxed: these are new challenge objectives for a different estimand. If tighter original precision is required, this design is insufficient.',
 'cluster_definition':'Independent resampling cluster is whole local unit. Episode cluster=(unit,scenario_id); non-episode cluster=(unit,UTC day). Subjects and episodes within a unit are dependent; never sum them as independent sample size.',
 'support_failure':'Retain first complete draw, publish only predeclared aggregate support PASS/FAIL before freeze, preserve detailed counts privately. Do not regenerate, relax rules, drop families, add events or change seeds. Failed technical correctness blocks all evaluation. Failed support blocks a full-family adequacy claim and automatic progression to feature/model work; a separate user decision may permit an explicitly qualified protocol without changing data/targets. Actual counts and failed objectives are released in the final frozen evaluation report, or in a separately authorized retirement audit after ending use as independent evidence, never as tuning feedback.',
 'no_prevalence_gate':'Challenge prevalence is measured, not targeted. No acceptance loop for class balance. Metrics undefined on empty classes are null with reasons; binary comparison requires both classes and adequate negative support.',
 'uncertainty_gate':'Support PASS alone does not establish adequate precision. If simultaneous family-recall interval width exceeds0.20, withhold a precise family conclusion even if counts pass; display estimate, counts and limitation. Arm/slice intervals require >=8 represented units; otherwise exploratory counts only.'}
write('challenge_support_policy.json',policy)

metrics={'primary':['accuracy','balanced_accuracy','macro_f1','suspicious_pattern_precision','suspicious_pattern_recall','suspicious_pattern_f1','ROC_AUC','PR_AUC_AP','false_positive_rate','domain_recall','family_recall','hard_negative_FPR'],
 'definitions':'Positive prediction score>=frozen threshold. Confusion [[TN,FP],[FN,TP]]. AP=sum recall increments*precision is the primary PR-AUC convention; call it Average Precision (AP), not trapezoidal area. Optionally show trapezoidal PR area clearly secondary. Family/domain recall=predicted positive among rows carrying frozen family/domain, including overlaps. Domain-only and unique multi-domain reported separately. Hard FPR=FP/(FP+TN) on union target0 in that origin/slice. Class0 recall=1-FPR.',
 'undefined':'Empty denominators => null plus raw numerator/denominator and reason. No predicted positives: precision0 with undefined flag; zero-denominator F1=0 flagged. ROC/AP with missing comparison class null. No imputed perfect scores.',
 'estimands':{'A':'Existing V4 Train/Validation development population; selected/reused development results, never independent final evidence.','B':'This enriched challenge law; report pooled predeclared equal-sized arms and each arm separately. Precision/AP describe realized challenge prevalence only. No pooling with V4 or natural-prevalence conversion. No population accuracy or operational PPV claim.'},
 'uncertainty':'10000 stratified whole-unit bootstrap replicates: sample 12 units with replacement within each arm, retain every event/subject/episode jointly; never independently bootstrap wallets or rows. Seed derived from sealed bootstrap stream. Percentile95% intervals overall; simultaneous twelve-family recall intervals use Bonferroni tails 0.025/12 and 1-0.025/12. Report per-unit counts, unit-equal mean recall/FPR as secondary, leave-one-unit-out ranges, and undefined bootstrap fraction. Suppress interval if >5% replicates undefined or fewer than8 supported units. Bootstrap intervals at 12 units/arm are approximate; they do not guarantee frequentist coverage.',
 'population_shift':'Report shifted minus reference metric differences with independent stratified unit bootstrap and same frozen model/threshold. Family-specific recall/FPR and availability changes accompany aggregate differences. No causal attribution to a single changed factor. Outcome does not trigger retraining.',
 'robustness':'Custodian reports missing/observed history strata and predefined near-boundary/hard-origin slices. For each of the frozen 40 semantic feature fields, permute that field across a fixed uniform3000-row sample within each arm, 3 repeats; use same baseline sample, signed AP drop and SD, absolute-mass shares. Permute transaction-type one-hot columns as one field. Diagnostic distributions may be off-manifold; importance is not causal and no maximum importance threshold is a success gate. No challenge retraining, feature selection or tuning. Optional matched-removal development models must fit within original36 slots and be frozen before access; if absent, report not measured.',
 'model_behaviour_success':{'status':'Proposed research acceptance criteria fixed by this protocol, not claims about safety or operational utility','conditions':['All technical/independence gates PASS and relevant support/precision objectives met','Pooled suspicious recall95% lower bound>=0.80','Each family simultaneous recall lower bound>=0.70','Each domain recall95% lower bound>=0.75','Overall FPR95% upper bound<=0.10','Each matched-hard FPR upper bound<=0.15; use simultaneous12-stratum Bonferroni bounds','Shifted arm family recall drop reference-minus-shifted upper95% bound<=0.15 for adequately supported families; unsupported differences INDETERMINATE'], 'logic':'Conjunction. Any definite failure => behavioural criterion not met. Missing/inadequate support => indeterminate, never PASS. Report every metric regardless. Macro F1 alone cannot establish success. These conservative illustrative synthetic-research tolerances require explicit protocol approval and are not derived from challenge outcomes.'}}
write('challenge_metrics_policy.json',metrics)

